    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.move\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen moving a visual selection with mini.move, there are three ways of making a visual selection:\r\n\r\nv to select character-wise\r\nV to select line-wise\r\nCtrl+v to select a block\r\n\r\nmini.move follows each visual selection accordingly, but It would be nice to have an option to make the line-wise (V) behaviour the default for every selection, since that's the default behaviour of every plugin/editor with similar functionality, and that's what I'm used to.\r\n\r\nThanks for working on mini.nvim!",
